# Character Studio MCP + CLI

Prefer the local job API over clicking the Studio window.

## Surfaces

| Surface | Location |
|---------|----------|
| API | `http://127.0.0.1:8765` (`app/app.py`, `--headless` ok) |
| Client | `app/agent_drive.py` |
| CLI | `runtime\python\python.exe app\cs_cli.py …` |
| MCP | `app/mcp_server.py` → tools `cs_*` (Cursor: `user-character-studio`) |

Details and `mcp.json` snippet: `AGENTS.md` § Agent drive.

## MCP first

1. `cs_ensure`
2. `cs_list_jobs` / `cs_get_job`
3. Edits: `cs_get_markers` → `cs_put_markers` → **zoom Markers + Skeleton/Rig on mesh** → `cs_see_skeleton`
4. Bind: `cs_run_step` `{ step: "rig", wait: true }`
5. Check: `cs_weights`, `cs_tears`, `cs_poses` (read the PNGs)

Also: `cs_run_step` for `markers` / `animations` / etc., `cs_stop`, `cs_rig_report`.

Never `cs_see_skeleton` or bind from numbers alone — see `marker-placement.mdc`.

## CLI equivalent

```powershell
cd D:\CharacterStudio\app
..\runtime\python\python.exe cs_cli.py ensure
..\runtime\python\python.exe cs_cli.py jobs
..\runtime\python\python.exe cs_cli.py run <job_id> rig --wait
..\runtime\python\python.exe cs_cli.py weights <job_id>
..\runtime\python\python.exe cs_cli.py tears <job_id>
```

If MCP is disconnected, use the CLI; do not fall back to desktop clicking unless the user asks for a visual the tools cannot provide.
